# StudyPilot v2 orchestrator rules

**Lead orchestrator:** read `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` and `docs/LEAD_ORCHESTRATOR.md` first. See also `.cursor/rules/lead-orchestrator.mdc`.

Before implementing, read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/orchestrator.md`, `eval/golden_set.jsonl`, and `docs/failures-checklist.md`.

## Delegation

- **Max 2–3 parallel writing agents.** More agents increase merge/review cost.
- **One file, one owner.** Never assign two agents to `retrieve.py`, `pipeline.py`, `ingestion.py`, or `models.py`.
- **Task card required:** allowed paths, forbidden paths, acceptance command (`.\scripts\phase_gate.ps1 -Phase <n>`).
- **Parallel Phase 1:** ingest (B) and retrieval (C) only after `docs/api-contracts.md` is frozen.

## Cursor subagent types

| Type | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `explore` | Read-only audits — golden set gaps, ingest quality, contract drift |
| `shell` | Docker, Alembic, pytest, `phase_gate.ps1`, `ingest_ppl.ps1` |
| `generalPurpose` | Single vertical slice with explicit file ownership |

Do not spawn subagents that edit the same paths concurrently.

## Forbidden without orchestrator

- Editing `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`
- Changing `docs/api-contracts.md` or Alembic schema during worker tasks
- Cross-editing another agent's owned directories
- New features before Phase 1c gate (precision@5 ≥ 70%, OOC 10/10)

## Gates

Human approves plan (Gate 1) and merge (Gate 2). Orchestrator runs `scripts/phase_gate.ps1` before merge.
